          "code": "RENDER_SUMMARY_WITH_ACTIONS",
          "id": "1772032024189",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772032024189_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an LLM node that generates a simple HTML snippet and, if available, a multiRecord widget  Follow these rules exactly:\n- Output the main HTML first, then optionally the multiRecordWidget. No markdown, no JSON, no explanations.\n- Use ONLY the data from {{$context.$nodes.EXCEPTION_DATA.$output.result}}.\n\n- The matched record is available at {{$context.$nodes.EXCEPTION_DATA.$output.result}}.\n  - Define matchedResult = {{$context.$nodes.EXCEPTION_DATA.$output.result}}.\n  - Define matchedException = matchedResult.exceptionDetails[0].\n  - If matchedResult is missing OR matchedResult.exceptionDetails is missing/empty, output exactly: <div class=\"order-exception-summary\"><p>No data found</p></div>\n\nCRITICAL HTML FORMATTING:\n- DO NOT use <br> tags anywhere (no \"<br\" substring anywhere).\n- Do NOT insert empty text nodes or blank lines.\n- Use only semantic block elements (h3, p, ul, li, div, strong, span).\n- Render HTML as a single root container: <div class=\"order-exception-summary\"> ... </div>\n- No icons, no emoji, no color instructions, and no icon-like characters (e.g., ✓, ✔, ✖). Use only bold text and punctuation/special characters like \"•\", \"—\", \":\".\n\nSAFETY/ACCURACY:\n- Escape HTML special characters in all values.\n- Do not fabricate data, product names, penalty totals, dates, or computed totals.\n- Do not introduce new numbers; you may only reuse numbers already present in the data.\n- Exclude/omit any field/line/list item/section whose mapped value does not exist in matchedResult (do not render placeholders and do not render empty elements).\n- It is allowed to output numbers exactly as they appear in the provided data values (e.g., \"$250\", \"1 day\"); do not calculate or create new numbers.\n\nDATA MAPPING (use these exact paths; do not pull from anywhere else):\n- Customer: matchedException.Customer\n- AccountType: matchedResult.CustomerInformation.AccountType\n- AnnualRevenue: matchedResult.CustomerInformation.AnnualRevenue\n- SalesAgreement: matchedResult.CustomerInformation.SalesAgreement\n- PenaltyClause: matchedResult.CustomerInformation.PenaltyClause\n- PenaltySummary: matchedResult.CustomerInformation.PenaltySummary\n- PenaltyDetails: matchedResult.CustomerInformation.PenaltyDetails\n- AdditionalDetails: matchedException.AdditionalDetails\n- RecommendedResolution: matchedException.RecommendedResolution.ResolutionSummary (use only if it exists and is a string; otherwise omit)\n- Outcome: matchedException.Outcome\n- SubstituteAccepted: matchedResult.OrderHistoryPattern.SubstituteAccepted\n- SplitsAccepted: matchedResult.OrderHistoryPattern.SplitsAccepted\n- DelayTolerance: matchedResult.OrderHistoryPattern.DelayTolerance\n- SplitsForReservationText: if matchedResult.OrderHistoryPattern.SplitsForReservation is exactly \"Y\", use \"Customer prefers split shipments.\"; otherwise use \"Customer doesn't prefer split shipments.\"- CostImpact: matchedResult.OutcomeDetails.CostImpact\n- SubstituteComparison: matchedResult.SubstituteComparison\n- AlternateResolutionDetails: matchedResult.AlternateResolutionDetails\n- Issue: matchedException.Issue\n\n\n##HTML STRUCTURE (strict order):\n\n\n0) Compact header line (deterministic segment join)\n- The first child element inside the root must be <h3>Exception Resolution Summary</h3>, followed immediately by a single <p> element.\n- Build an ordered list named headerSegments. Add segments in this exact order ONLY if the mapped value exists and is a string and trim() is not empty:\n  1) CustomerSegment: <strong>{Customer}</strong>\n  2) AccountTypeSegment: <span>{AccountType}</span>\n  3) SalesAgreementSegment: <span>SA: {SalesAgreement}</span>\n  4) LifetimeValueSegment: <span>Lifetime Value: {AnnualRevenue}</span>\n- IMPORTANT: If AccountType exists at matchedResult.CustomerInformation.AccountType and is a non-empty string, it MUST be included as AccountTypeSegment (do not omit it).\n- Render the <p> by joining headerSegments with <span> — </span> (use the separator only between present segments).\n- If only CustomerSegment exists, render only the <strong>Customer</strong> without separators.\n\n1) Risk block (headline + one bullet)\n- Output the risk-callout ONLY if PenaltyDetails exists OR PenaltyClause exists.\n- Construct RiskHeadline as plain text using the mapped values (no curly-brace templating; use values verbatim and escape HTML):\n  - If PenaltyDetails exists AND PenaltyClause exists: RiskHeadline = PenaltyDetails + \" - Penalty Clause \" + PenaltyClause\n  - Else if only PenaltyDetails exists: RiskHeadline = PenaltyDetails\n  - Else if only PenaltyClause exists: RiskHeadline = \"Penalty Clause \" + PenaltyClause\n- Construct RiskBullet as plain text using the mapped values (no curly-brace templating; use values verbatim and escape HTML):\n  - If PenaltySummary exists AND DelayTolerance exists: RiskBullet = PenaltySummary + \" beyond the \" + DelayTolerance + \" delay tolerance\"\n  - Else if only PenaltySummary exists: RiskBullet = PenaltySummary\n  - Else RiskBullet does not exist.\n- Render:\n  <div class=\"risk-callout\">\n    <p class=\"risk-headline\"><strong></strong></p>\n    <p><strong>{{RiskHeadline}}</strong></p>\n    {{#if RiskBullet}}\n    <ul><li><strong>{{RiskBullet}}</strong></li></ul>\n    {{/if}}\n  </div>\n\n2) Customer History (title case)\n- If matchedException.ErrorCode === \"DOO_INV_NO_RESERVATION_REQ_QTY\":\n  - Output <h3>Customer History</h3> ONLY if SplitsForReservationText exists.\n  - Render ONLY:\n    - <li><span>{{SplitsForReservationText}}</span></li>\n  - Do NOT render SubstituteAccepted, SplitsAccepted, or DelayTolerance.\n\n- If matchedException.ErrorCode != \"DOO_INV_NO_RESERVATION_REQ_QTY\"::\n  - Output <h3>Customer History</h3> ONLY if at least one of SubstituteAccepted, SplitsAccepted, or DelayTolerance exists.\n  - Then a <ul> containing only the <li> items whose values exist:\n    - <li><strong>Substitutes:</strong> <span>{{SubstituteAccepted}}</span></li>\n    - <li><strong>Splits:</strong> <span>{{SplitsAccepted}}</span></li>\n    - <li><strong>Delay Tolerance:</strong> <span>{{DelayTolerance}}</span></li>\n  - Do NOT render SplitsForReservationText.\n\n3) Recommended Resolution (title case)\n- Output <h3>Recommended Resolution</h3> ONLY if at least one of RecommendedResolution, CostImpact, Outcome exists.\n- Then a <ul> containing only the <li> items whose values exist:\n  - <li><strong>Action:</strong> <span>{{RecommendedResolution}}</span></li>\n  - <li><strong>Cost Impact:</strong> <span>{{CostImpact}}</span></li>\n  - <li><strong>Outcome:</strong> <span>{{Outcome}}</span></li>\n\n- This section must always render after Customer History.\n\n4) SubstituteComparison **multiRecordWidget**\n\nLet `SC = SubstituteComparison`.\n\n**Validate first (before generating any widget-related content):**\n- If `SC` is missing, null, not an object, is an array, or is an empty object: output nothing for this widget.\n\n**Eligibility (must pass to generate anything):**\n- Only proceed if BOTH fields exist and are non-blank after trimming:\n  - `SC.OriginalItemDescription`\n  - `SC.SubstituteItemDescription`\n\n**If eligibility fails:**\n- Output nothing for this widget (do not mention `multiRecordWidget`, do not emit cols/rows/cells/badges, do not emit placeholders).\n\n**If eligibility passes:**\nUse a **multiRecordWidget** with cols **\"Item\"**, **\"Availability\"**, **\"Description\"**, and **\"ETA\"** to display exactly **two rows** (Original then Substitute).\n\nRow 1 (Original):\n- Item = `SC.OriginalItemDescription`\n- Availability = badge text **\"Out of Stock\"**, priority **\"alert\"**\n- Description = `SC.OriginalItemLongDescription` (only if non-blank; otherwise omit)\n- ETA = `SC.OriginalItemETA` (only if non-blank; otherwise omit)\n\nRow 2 (Substitute):\n- Item = `SC.SubstituteItemDescription`\n- Availability = badge text **\"Available\"**, priority **\"success\"**\n- Description = `SC.SubstituteItemLongDescription` (only if non-blank; otherwise omit)\n- ETA = `SC.SubstituteItemETA` (only if non-blank; otherwise omit)\n\n**Strict source rule (no inference / no fallback):**\n- Populate values only from the `SC.*` fields listed above.\n- Do not use any other payload fields to fill gaps.\n\n5) Generate an Actionable Insight\nGenerate an actionable insight for the Recommended Resolution using the following rules:\n- title: \"Apply Recommendation\"\n- actionText: \"Apply Recommendation\"\n- followUpCommand:\n  - If matchedException.RecommendedResolutionPayload.updateSchedulingAttributes exists as a non-empty array:\n    `ora.Agent({\"actionType\":\"performResolution\",\"resolutionType\":matchedException.RecommendedResolution.ResolutionType,\"data\":matchedException.RecommendedResolutionPayload.updateSchedulingAttributes,\"HeaderId\":matchedException.HeaderId,\"FulfillLineId\":matchedException.FulfillLineId, \"ErrorCode\":matchedException.ErrorCode})`\n  - Else if matchedException.RecommendedResolutionPayload.updateAttributes exists as a non-empty array:\n    `ora.Agent({\"actionType\":\"performResolution\",\"resolutionType\":matchedException.RecommendedResolution.ResolutionType,\"data\":matchedException.RecommendedResolutionPayload.updateAttributes,\"HeaderId\":matchedException.HeaderId,\"FulfillLineId\":matchedException.FulfillLineId, \"ErrorCode\":matchedException.ErrorCode})`\n  - Else:\n    `ora.Agent({\"actionType\":\"performResolution\",\"data\":{}})`\n\n\n6) Generate an Actionable Insight\n**Validate first (before generating 'actionable insight' content):**\n- If `AlternateResolutionDetails` is missing, null, not an object, is an array, or is an empty object: output nothing for this Actionable Insight.\n\n**Eligibility (must pass to generate anything):**\n- Only proceed when `AlternateResolutionDetails` has minimum or at least 1 record.\n\n**If eligibility fails:**\n- Output nothing for this Actionable Insight (do not mention `Actionable Insight`, do not emit placeholders).\n\n**If eligibility passes:**\nGenerate an actionable insight for the Viewing Alternate Resolutions using following the options: \n  title:\"Modify\".\n  followUpCommand:  - Must be exactly:\n  - `ora.Agent({\"actionType\":\"modifyResolutions\", \"data\":`exception.FulfillLineId`, \"FulfillLineId\":exception.FulfillLineId`})`\n  actionText must be \"Modify\".\n\n\n#Final Mandatory Instructions\n1. No <br> and no \"<br\" substring anywhere in the output; no blank lines.\n2. Dont Render HTML tags in any of the widgets related fields\n3. Do not Render anything after </oraInfoDisplay>\n4. Don't render **Titles** for the widget\n5. Mandate returning HTML prompt if any HTML related data exists.\n6. Mandate returning the \"Apply Recommendation\" actionable insight if RecommendedResolution exists.\n7. Mandate returning the \"Modify\" actionable insight if AlternateResolutionDetails exists and is valid.\n8. Render Actionable Insight only within <oraInsight>; never place it inside <oraInfoDisplay>. The <oraInsight> block must appear after the closing </oraInfoDisplay>.\n9. Render all HTML content strictly before the opening <oraInfoDisplay> tag."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Exception Data",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const targetFulfillLineId = String($context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_PAYLOAD.$output.result.data);\nconst outputArray = $context.$variables.pCuratedData?.outputArray || [];\n\nlet matchedResult = null;\n\nfor (const entry of outputArray) {\n  const result = entry?.result;\n  const exceptionDetails = result?.exceptionDetails || [];\n\n  let hasMatch = false;\n\n  for (const ex of exceptionDetails) {\n    const rr = ex?.RecommendedResolution || {};\n    const rrp = ex?.RecommendedResolutionPayload || {};\n\n    // Special handling for Alternate Warehouse\n    if (String(rr?.ResolutionType) === \"Alternate Warehouse\") {\n      const schedulingAttrs = Array.isArray(rrp.updateSchedulingAttributes)\n        ? rrp.updateSchedulingAttributes\n        : [];\n\n      for (const a of schedulingAttrs) {\n        const requests = Array.isArray(a?.requests) ? a.requests : [];\n        for (const req of requests) {\n          if (String(req?.FulfillLineId) === targetFulfillLineId) {\n            hasMatch = true;\n            break;\n          }\n        }\n        if (hasMatch) break;\n      }\n    } else {\n      // Existing generic handling\n      const schedulingAttrs = Array.isArray(rrp.updateSchedulingAttributes)\n        ? rrp.updateSchedulingAttributes\n        : [];\n\n      for (const a of schedulingAttrs) {\n        if (String(a?.FulfillLineId) === targetFulfillLineId) {\n          hasMatch = true;\n          break;\n        }\n\n        const requests = Array.isArray(a?.requests) ? a.requests : [];\n        for (const req of requests) {\n          if (String(req?.FulfillLineId) === targetFulfillLineId) {\n            hasMatch = true;\n            break;\n          }\n        }\n        if (hasMatch) break;\n      }\n\n      if (hasMatch) break;\n\n      const updateAttrs = Array.isArray(rrp.updateAttributes)\n        ? rrp.updateAttributes\n        : [];\n\n      for (const a of updateAttrs) {\n        const innerRequests = Array.isArray(a?.requests) ? a.requests : [];\n        for (const req of innerRequests) {\n          if (String(req?.FulfillLineId) === targetFulfillLineId) {\n            hasMatch = true;\n            break;\n          }\n        }\n        if (hasMatch) break;\n      }\n    }\n\n    if (hasMatch) break;\n  }\n\n  if (hasMatch) {\n    matchedResult = result;\n    break;\n  }\n}\n\nreturn matchedResult;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772032024189"
          },
          "code": "EXCEPTION_DATA",
