        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": true,
              "customNotes": "Generate a MessageList Widget and an Email Communication as per the provided instructions"
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Modify Resolutions From Query Mode"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "MODIFY_RESOLUTIONS_FROM_QUERY_MODE",
          "id": "1772173401263",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772173401264_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an LLM node that generates a messageListWidget. Follow these rules exactly:\n- Use ONLY the data from {{$context.$nodes.EXCEPTION_DATA_FOR_MODIFY_RESOLUTION.$output.result}}.\n\n- The matched record is available at {{$context.$nodes.EXCEPTION_DATA_FOR_MODIFY_RESOLUTION.$output.result}}.\n  - Define matchedResult = {{$context.$nodes.EXCEPTION_DATA_FOR_MODIFY_RESOLUTION.$output.result}}.\n  - Define matchedException = matchedResult.exceptionDetails[0].\n  - If matchedResult is missing OR matchedResult.exceptionDetails is missing/empty, output exactly: <div class=\"order-exception-summary\"><p>No data found</p></div>\n\nDATA MAPPING (use these exact paths; do not pull from anywhere else):\n- Customer: matchedException.Customer\n- AccountType: matchedResult.CustomerInformation.AcccountType\n- AnnualRevenue: matchedResult.CustomerInformation.AnnualRevenue\n- SalesAgreement: matchedResult.CustomerInformation.SalesAgreement\n- PenaltyClause: matchedResult.CustomerInformation.PenaltyClause\n- PenaltySummary: matchedResult.CustomerInformation.PenaltySummary\n- PenaltyDetails: matchedResult.CustomerInformation.PenaltyDetails\n- AdditionalDetails: matchedException.AdditionalDetails\n- RecommendedResolution: matchedException.RecommendedResolution.ResolutionSummary (use only if it exists and is a string; otherwise omit)\n- RecommendedResolutionPayload: matchedException.RecommendedResolutionPayload\n- Outcome: matchedException.Outcome\n- SubstituteAccepted: matchedResult.OrderHistoryPattern.SubstituteAccepted\n- SplitsAccepted: matchedResult.OrderHistoryPattern.SplitsAccepted\n- DelayTolerance: matchedResult.OrderHistoryPattern.DelayTolerance\n- CostImpact: matchedResult.OutcomeDetails.CostImpact\n- SubstituteComparison: matchedResult.SubstituteComparison\n- AlternateResolutionDetails: matchedResult.AlternateResolutionDetails\n\n\n##Generate messageListWidget (AlternateResolutionDetails):\n- Don't render any title for this widget.\n- Immediately after the multiRecordWidget, if AlternateResolutionDetails exists and has one or more rows, output a messageListWidget.\n- Data source: rows = AlternateResolutionDetails array. Preserve source order.\nPer-row field mapping (each field is emitted as Field: value; not JSON):\n- Title: \"\"\n- Summary: row.ReasonForLowPriority (omit if missing).\n- Subtitle: row.Summary (use as-is; do not invent or add new numbers).\n- badgeText: \"Accept Recommendation\"\n- Priority: medium\n- Action must include ALL rows from row.ResolutionPayload (preserve source order).\n\nExact emission format:\nUse a messageListWidget\nTitle: <null value>\nSubtitle: <value>\nSummary: <value>\nbadgeText: <value>\nPriority: <value>\nAction:\n- If row.ResolutionPayload.updateSchedulingAttributes exists as a non-empty array:\n  `ora.Agent({\"actionType\":\"performResolution\",\"resolutionType\":row.ResolutionType,\"data\":row.ResolutionPayload.updateSchedulingAttributes,\"HeaderId\":matchedException.HeaderId,\"FulfillLineId\":matchedException.FulfillLineId,\"ErrorCode\":matchedException.ErrorCode)`\n- Else if row.ResolutionPayload.updateAttributes exists as a non-empty array:\n  `ora.Agent({\"actionType\":\"performResolution\",\"resolutionType\":row.ResolutionType,\"data\":row.ResolutionPayload.updateAttributes,\"HeaderId\":matchedException.HeaderId,\"FulfillLineId\":matchedException.FulfillLineId,\"ErrorCode\":matchedException.ErrorCode})`\n- Else:\n  `ora.Agent({\"actionType\":\"performResolution\",\"data\":{}})`\n\n## Generate one Email Communication\n\nGenerate One Email Communication for below (**IT IS IMPORTANT AND NON-NEGOTIABLE TO GENERATE Email Communication):\n**Always generate the Communications irrespective of the Recommended Resolution.\nUse simple HTML only (<p>, <b>, <br/>). No raw JSON in the body. No internal field names. No cross-order references. No speculative statements.\n\n### Derive variables/placeholders FIRST (outside oraComms)\n\nIssue source:\n- Issue = matchedException.Issue\n- SSD source = matchedException.DelayedScheduledShipDate\n\n<issueType>\nDetermine issueType using STRICT keyword rules (case-insensitive). DO NOT GUESS:\n- If Issue contains the word \"Backordered\" anywhere => issueType = \"BACKORDERED\"\n- Else if Issue contains the phrase \"out of stock\" anywhere => issueType = \"OUT_OF_STOCK\"\n- Else if Issue contains the phrase \"Reservation\" anywhere => issueType = \"RESERVATION_ISSUE\"\n- Else => issueType = \"UNKNOWN\"\n\nMANDATORY ROUTING:\n- If issueType = BACKORDERED you MUST use the \"Supplier Date Change\" email.\n- If issueType = OUT_OF_STOCK you MUST use the \"Item Unavailable\" email.\n</issueType>\n\n<ITEM>\nDerive ITEM from matchedException.Issue:\n\nIf issueType = \"OUT_OF_STOCK\":\n  ITEM = substring before \"is out of stock\" (trim)\n  If ITEM is empty or equals \"Item\" (case-insensitive), ITEM = \"your item\"\n\nIf issueType = \"BACKORDERED\":\n  Remove \"Backordered\" (trim)\n  Remove trailing \"(Line N)\" if present (trim)\n  If it matches \"<number> of <rest>\", keep only \"<rest>\"\n  Trim result\n  If empty or equals \"Line\" (case-insensitive), ITEM = \"your item\"\n\n\nIf issueType = \"RESERVATION_ISSUE\":\n  Remove prefix \"Reservation failure:\" (trim)\n  Remove trailing \"(Line N)\" if present (trim)\n  If it matches \"Ordered quantity <number> <unit> of <item>\":\n    ITEM = \"<item>\"\n  Else if it matches \"<number> of <rest>\":\n    ITEM = \"<rest>\"\n  Else:\n    ITEM = remaining string\n  Trim ITEM\n  If ITEM is empty or equals \"Line\" (case-insensitive):\n    ITEM = \"your item\"\n\n\nIf issueType = \"UNKNOWN\":\n  ITEM = \"your item\"\n</ITEM>\n\n<SSD>\nSSD = matchedException.DelayedScheduledShipDate\nIf SSD is missing/empty: SSD = \"the next available ship date\"\nElse: render SSD. If SSD cannot be reliably parsed as a date, use SSD as-is.\n</SSD>\n\n\n\n<emailSubject>\nSubject must acknowledge a delay, vary by issueType, include OrderNumber and ITEM, and must NOT include SSD.\n\nIf issueType = \"OUT_OF_STOCK\":\n  Update on your order {{$context.$nodes.EXCEPTION_DATA_FOR_MODIFY_RESOLUTION.$output.result.exceptionDetails[0].OrderNumber}}: Item unavailable — <ITEM> delayed\nElse if issueType = \"BACKORDERED\":\n  Update on your order {{$context.$nodes.EXCEPTION_DATA_FOR_MODIFY_RESOLUTION.$output.result.exceptionDetails[0].OrderNumber}}: Supplier date change — <ITEM> delayed\nElse If issueType = \"RESERVATION_ISSUE\":\n  Update on your order {{$context.$nodes.EXCEPTION_DATA_FOR_MODIFY_RESOLUTION.$output.result.exceptionDetails[0].OrderNumber}}: Item unavailable — <ITEM> delayed\nElse:\n  Update on your order {{$context.$nodes.EXCEPTION_DATA_FOR_MODIFY_RESOLUTION.$output.result.exceptionDetails[0].OrderNumber}}: Shipment delayed — <ITEM>\n</emailSubject>\n\n<emailContentHtml>\nRULES:\n- Treat \"Dear <name>,\" as the email header.\n- Treat \"Regards, <full name>\" as the email footer.\n- Do not add any extra text before the greeting or after the signature.\n- Do not output the words \"HEADER\" or \"FOOTER\" in the final content.\n\nHEADER: \nDear {{$context.$nodes.GET_CUSTOMER_NAME.$output.result}} , \n\nBODY:\nIf issueType = \"OUT_OF_STOCK\":\n  <p>We would like to inform you that your ordered item <b>&lt;ITEM&gt;</b> is currently delayed. \n  We sincerely apologize for the inconvenience and appreciate your patience. Please let us know if you have any questions or require further assistance.</p>\n\nElse if issueType = \"BACKORDERED\":\n  <p>We would like to inform you that the shipment of your item <b>&lt;ITEM&gt;</b> has been delayed due to a change in schedule from our supplier. The revised ship date is <b>&lt;SSD&gt;</b>.<br/><br/>\n  We apologize for the inconvenience and appreciate your understanding. Please feel free to reach out if you need any additional information.</p>\n\nElse If issueType = \"RESERVATION_ISSUE\":\n  <p>We would like to inform you that your ordered item <b>&lt;ITEM&gt;</b> is not available.\n  We sincerely apologize for the inconvenience and appreciate your patience. Please let us know if you have any questions or require further assistance.</p>\n\nElse:\n  <p>We would like to inform you that your item <b>&lt;ITEM&gt;</b> is currently delayed. The revised earliest ship date is <b>&lt;SSD&gt;</b>.<br/><br/>\n  We apologize for the inconvenience and appreciate your patience. Please let us know if you have any questions or require further assistance.</p>\n\nFOOTER:\nRegards,\n{{$context.$app.$OraUserContext.fullName}} \n\n</emailContentHtml>\n\n\n### Communication Insight (oraComms) - reference derived placeholders\n\n<oraComms>\n{\n  \"title\": \"Acknowledge Delay\",\n  \"shortDescription\": <A concise, one-line summary of the resolution options>,\n  \"actionText\": \"Send Email\",\n  \"type\": \"email\",\n  \"content\": \"<emailContentHtml>\",\n  \"params\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"email\",\n      \"title\": \"email address\",\n      \"defaultValue\": {{$context.$nodes.GET_CUSTOMER_EMAIL_ADDRESS.$output.result}}\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"subject\",\n      \"title\": \"Subject\",\n      \"defaultValue\": \"<emailSubject>\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n</oraComms>\n\nIMPORTANT NOTE:\n- Always generate the Communication Insight without fail for user to send email.\n- Do not keep the generated email content as free flowing text; it must be assigned to \"content\" in oraComms.\n\n#Final Mandatory Instructions\n1. No <br> and no \"<br\" substring anywhere in the output; no blank lines.\n2. Dont Render HTML tags in any of the widgets related fields\n3. Do not render anything after </oraInfoDisplay> except the required <oraComms> block.\n4. Don't render **Titles** for any of the 2 widget\n5. Always Return an Email Communication i.e., Contents under <oraComms> are always returned.\n6. After rendering </oraInfoDisplay>, render exactly one <oraComms> block immediately after it.\n7. Do not render any text, punctuation, whitespace-only commentary, markdown, or any other tags after </oraComms>.\n8. The final output must contain only the <oraInfoDisplay> block followed by the <oraComms> block, with nothing else outside them."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Exception Data For Modify Resolution",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const targetFulfillLineId = String($context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_PAYLOAD.$output.result.data);\nconst outputArray = $context.$variables.pCuratedData?.outputArray || [];\n\nlet matchedResult = null;\n\nfor (const entry of outputArray) {\n  const result = entry?.result;\n  const exceptionDetails = result?.exceptionDetails || [];\n\n  let hasMatch = false;\n\n  for (const ex of exceptionDetails) {\n\n    const rr = ex?.RecommendedResolution || {};\n    const rrp = ex?.RecommendedResolutionPayload || {};\n\n    // ---- SPLIT / ALTERNATE WAREHOUSE (updateSchedulingAttributes) ----\n    const schedAttrs = Array.isArray(rrp.updateSchedulingAttributes)\n      ? rrp.updateSchedulingAttributes\n      : [];\n\n    for (const a of schedAttrs) {\n\n      // Case 1: direct FulfillLineId (existing behavior)\n      if (String(a?.FulfillLineId) === targetFulfillLineId) {\n        hasMatch = true;\n        break;\n      }\n\n      // Case 2: Alternate Warehouse → inside requests[]\n      const reqs = Array.isArray(a?.requests) ? a.requests : [];\n      for (const r of reqs) {\n        if (String(r?.FulfillLineId) === targetFulfillLineId) {\n          hasMatch = true;\n          break;\n        }\n      }\n\n      if (hasMatch) break;\n    }\n\n    if (hasMatch) break;\n\n    // ---- RESERVE / CANCEL (updateAttributes -> requests) ----\n    const updAttrs = Array.isArray(rrp.updateAttributes)\n      ? rrp.updateAttributes\n      : [];\n\n    for (const u of updAttrs) {\n      const reqs = Array.isArray(u?.requests) ? u.requests : [];\n      for (const r of reqs) {\n        if (String(r?.FulfillLineId) === targetFulfillLineId) {\n          hasMatch = true;\n          break;\n        }\n      }\n      if (hasMatch) break;\n    }\n\n    if (hasMatch) break;\n  }\n\n  if (hasMatch) {\n    matchedResult = result;\n    break;\n  }\n}\n\nreturn matchedResult;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774343627288"
          },
          "code": "EXCEPTION_DATA_FOR_MODIFY_RESOLUTION",
          "id": "1772174331450",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Fetch Exception Details for Display",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const outputArray = Array.isArray($context.$variables.pCuratedData?.outputArray)\n  ? $context.$variables.pCuratedData.outputArray\n  : [];\n\n/*const curated = $context.$variables.pCuratedData ?? {};\n\n// Support either:\n// 1) pCuratedData = [ { result: ... }, ... ]\n// 2) pCuratedData = { exceptionDetails: [...], ... }\nconst outputArray = Array.isArray(curated)\n  ? curated\n  : Array.isArray(curated.outputArray)\n    ? curated.outputArray\n    : Array.isArray(curated.exceptionDetails)\n      ? [{ result: curated }]\n      : [];*/\n\nconst toNumber = (v) => {\n  if (v === null || v === undefined) return null;\n  if (typeof v === \"number\" && Number.isFinite(v)) return v;\n  if (typeof v === \"string\") {\n    // remove commas, currency symbols, and spaces\n    const cleaned = v.replace(/[$,]/g, \"\").trim();\n    const n = Number(cleaned);\n    return Number.isFinite(n) ? n : null;\n  }\n  return null;\n};\n\nconst pick = (obj, keys) => {\n  const out = {};\n  keys.forEach((k) => {\n    out[k] = obj?.[k] ?? null;\n  });\n  return out;\n};\n\n// Keep ONLY what UI needs (no large nested payloads)\nconst UI_FIELDS = [\n  \"OrderNumber\",\n  \"Customer\",\n  \"Issue\",\n  \"Impact\",\n  \"AdditionalDetails\",\n  \"FulfillLineId\",\n  \"Outcome\",\n  \"LineTotal\",\n  \"RecommendedResolution\",\n];\n\nconst exceptions = [];\n\nfor (const item of outputArray) {\n  const parent = item?.result ?? item;\n  // Ignore empty result\n  if (!parent || (typeof parent === \"object\" && Object.keys(parent).length === 0)) continue;\n\n  const exceptionDetails = Array.isArray(parent?.exceptionDetails) ? parent.exceptionDetails : [];\n  if (exceptionDetails.length === 0) continue;\n\n  for (const ex of exceptionDetails) {\n    const exObj = ex && typeof ex === \"object\" ? ex : {};\n    // Prefer values from ex; if missing, fall back to parent (just in case)\n    const merged = {\n      ...exObj,\n      Outcome: exObj.Outcome ?? parent?.Outcome ?? null,\n      LineTotal: exObj.LineTotal ?? parent?.LineTotal ?? null,\n    };\n    // Build a UI-safe flattened row\n    const row = pick(merged, UI_FIELDS);\n    // Add numeric form for severity computation (optional but recommended)\n    row.LineTotalNum = toNumber(row.LineTotal);\n    // Also flatten RecommendedResolution text helpers (optional, keeps original object intact)\nconst isNoReservationQty =\n  exObj?.ErrorCode?.trim() === \"DOO_INV_NO_RESERVATION_REQ_QTY\";\n\n    /*row.RecommendedResolutionType = row.RecommendedResolution?.ResolutionType ?? null;\n    row.RecommendedResolutionSummary = row.RecommendedResolution?.ResolutionSummary ?? null;\n    row.ErrorCode = exObj.ErrorCode;*/\n/*row.RecommendedResolutionDisplay =\n  exObj?.ErrorCode === \"DOO_INV_NO_RESERVATION_REQ_QTY\"\n    ? row.RecommendedResolution?.ResolutionSummary ?? null\n    : row.RecommendedResolution?.ResolutionType && row.RecommendedResolution?.ResolutionSummary\n      ? `${row.RecommendedResolution.ResolutionType} — ${row.RecommendedResolution.ResolutionSummary}`\n      : row.RecommendedResolution?.ResolutionType\n        || row.RecommendedResolution?.ResolutionSummary\n        || null;\n*/\nrow.RecommendedResolutionDisplay =\n  row.RecommendedResolution?.ResolutionSummary ?? null;\n    exceptions.push(row);\n  }\n}\n\n/**\n * SUMMARY (fail-safe only)\n * - Compute a single SummaryTitle string, but if anything fails at runtime,\n *   leave it blank (\"\") rather than throwing or producing partial output.\n * - Pad it as a flattened field on every exception row.\n */\nlet summaryTitle = \"\";\ntry {\n  const critical = exceptions.filter(\n    (e) => typeof e.LineTotalNum === \"number\" && e.LineTotalNum >= 30000\n  );\n\n  const criticalCount = critical.length;\n  const criticalImpact = critical.reduce((sum, e) => sum + e.LineTotalNum, 0);\n\n\n  const impactStr = String(Math.trunc(criticalImpact));\n  summaryTitle =\n    criticalCount === 0\n      ? `${exceptions.length} exceptions`\n      : `${criticalCount} ${criticalCount === 1 ? \"Critical issue\" : \"Critical issues\"} impacting $${impactStr}`;\n\n\n} catch (e) {\n  summaryTitle = \"\";\n}\n\nfor (const ex of exceptions) {\n  ex.SummaryTitle = summaryTitle;\n}\n\nexceptions.sort((a, b) => {\n  const aLineTotal = a.LineTotalNum ?? Number.NEGATIVE_INFINITY;\n  const bLineTotal = b.LineTotalNum ?? Number.NEGATIVE_INFINITY;\n\n  return bLineTotal - aLineTotal;\n});\n\nreturn { exceptions };"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771477805676"
          },
          "code": "FETCH_EXCEPTION_DETAILS_FOR_DISPLAY",
          "id": "1772340563885",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Fetch Payload For Actions",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const outputArray = Array.isArray($context.$variables.pCuratedData?.outputArray)\n  ? $context.$variables.pCuratedData.outputArray\n  : [];\n\n/*const curated = $context.$variables.pCuratedData ?? {};\n\n// Support either:\n// 1) pCuratedData = [ { result: ... }, ... ]\n// 2) pCuratedData = { exceptionDetails: [...], ... }\nconst outputArray = Array.isArray(curated)\n  ? curated\n  : Array.isArray(curated.outputArray)\n    ? curated.outputArray\n    : Array.isArray(curated.exceptionDetails)\n      ? [{ result: curated }]\n      : [];\n\n*/\n\nconst toNumber = (v) => {\n  if (v === null || v === undefined) return null;\n  if (typeof v === \"number\" && Number.isFinite(v)) return v;\n  if (typeof v === \"string\") {\n    // remove commas, currency symbols, and spaces\n    const cleaned = v.replace(/[$,]/g, \"\").trim();\n    const n = Number(cleaned);\n    return Number.isFinite(n) ? n : null;\n  }\n  return null;\n};\n\nconst exceptions = [];\n\nfor (const item of outputArray) {\n  const parent = item?.result ?? item;\n  if (!parent || typeof parent !== \"object\") continue;\n\n  const exceptionDetails = Array.isArray(parent.exceptionDetails)\n    ? parent.exceptionDetails\n    : [];\n\n  for (const ex of exceptionDetails) {\n    const rr = ex?.RecommendedResolution ?? null;\n    const rrp = ex?.RecommendedResolutionPayload ?? null;\n    const hdrId = ex?.HeaderId ?? null;\n    const flineId = ex?.FulfillLineId ?? null;\n    const errorCode = ex?.ErrorCode ?? null;\n    const lineTotal = ex.LineTotal ?? parent?.LineTotal ?? null;\n    const lineTotalNum = toNumber(lineTotal);\n\n    exceptions.push({\n      ResolutionSummary: rr?.ResolutionSummary ?? null,\n      ResolutionType: rr?.ResolutionType ?? null,\n      OrderNumber: ex?.OrderNumber ?? null,\n      Customer: ex?.Customer ?? null,\n      HeaderId: hdrId,\n      FulfillLineId: flineId,\n      LineTotal: lineTotalNum,\n      ErrorCode: errorCode,\n      updateSchedulingAttributes: Array.isArray(rrp?.updateSchedulingAttributes)\n        ? rrp.updateSchedulingAttributes\n        : [],\n      updateAttributes: Array.isArray(rrp?.updateAttributes)\n        ? rrp.updateAttributes\n        : []\n    });\n  }\n}\n\nexceptions.sort((a, b) => {\n  const aLineTotal = a.LineTotal ?? Number.NEGATIVE_INFINITY;\n  const bLineTotal = b.LineTotal ?? Number.NEGATIVE_INFINITY;\n\n  return bLineTotal - aLineTotal;\n});\n\nreturn { exceptions };"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771560872613"
          },
          "code": "FETCH_PAYLOAD_FOR_ACTIONS",
          "id": "1772340681892",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
